WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.083
Legion took this issue to done:

00:00:03.428 --> 00:00:04.669
checked in production,

00:00:05.341 --> 00:00:06.327
and signed off.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.057
To hand Legion an issue,

00:00:09.753 --> 00:00:10.897
add the legion label

00:00:12.039 --> 00:00:13.832
and set it to Todo.

00:00:14.008 --> 00:00:16.313
Legion admits it and claims it.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.886
The architect's questions come to your Inbox.

00:00:21.229 --> 00:00:21.993
Pick an answer,

00:00:23.182 --> 00:00:24.843
and once every one is answered,

00:00:25.437 --> 00:00:28.023
it asks you to approve the spec.

00:00:29.657 --> 00:00:30.233
Approve it,

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:31.489
and it's clear.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:37.071
The status follows each phase.

00:00:39.801 --> 00:00:41.576
READY names the pull request,

00:00:41.898 --> 00:00:44.222
and what it changes, for your merge.

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:50.764
From the terminal, legion state reads the daemon;

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.681
its JSON shows the architect, ready;

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:59.291
legion claims list shows each claim.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:01.920
Then start the controller.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:05.505
It checks the controller's Oh My Pi,

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:06.720
then starts it.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:10.291
The controller opens on its start procedure,

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:14.220
and registers with the daemon.
